+# 20260707-0850 — Real diff Claude Code VS Code ext 2.1.201 → 2.1.202
+
+Verified diff between the two **pristine** VSIX extracts (no patches
+applied). All observations below rely on direct string extraction from
+`vendor/anthropic.claude-code/v2.1.201-pristine/` and `.../v2.1.202-pristine/`.
+
+**Empty checks first** — these did NOT change :
+
+- `package.json` : only the `"version"` field bumped (`2.1.201` →
+  `2.1.202`). All other schema keys, enums, command contributions,
+  activation events identical.
+- `claude-code-settings.schema.json` : only the auto-generated
+  `"$comment": "Generated on <date>"` timestamp changed.
+- Command surface : **0 new commands** registered, **0 removed**.
+- Enum values : `preferredLocation` still `["sidebar", "panel"]` on
+  both. Anthropic has NOT added `"primary"` natively — that was a
+  false alarm from an earlier diff against a self-patched v2.1.202.
+- Extension activation events : identical.
+- Contributed keybindings : identical.
+- Contributed views : identical.
+- Contributed walkthroughs, icons, resources except `native-binary/claude`
+  (see below).
+
+## What actually changed
+
+### 1. Cloud provider support — AWS Bedrock + GCP Vertex
+
+35+ new string literals in `extension.js`, all cloud-credential /
+metadata related. The extension now speaks Bedrock and Vertex natively
+via env-var detection.
+
+**AWS Bedrock** — 14 new env-var names read at runtime :
+
+```
+AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID              AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY       AWS_SESSION_TOKEN
+AWS_REGION                     AWS_DEFAULT_REGION          AWS_PROFILE
+AWS_CONFIG_FILE                AWS_SHARED_CREDENTIALS_FILE
+AWS_CONTAINER_CREDENTIALS_FULL_URI        AWS_CONTAINER_CREDENTIALS_RELATIVE_URI
+AWS_CONTAINER_AUTHORIZATION_TOKEN         AWS_CONTAINER_AUTHORIZATION_TOKEN_FILE
+AWS_EC2_METADATA_SERVICE_ENDPOINT         AWS_EC2_METADATA_SERVICE_ENDPOINT_MODE
+```
+
+**GCP Vertex** — 7 new env-var names + metadata service :
+
+```
+GCE_METADATA_HOST              GCE_METADATA_IP             METADATA_SERVER_DETECTION
+GCLOUD_PROJECT                 GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT        GOOGLE_CLOUD_QUOTA_PROJECT
+GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS
+```
+
+**Vertex model regions** — one constant per model family :
+
+```
+VERTEX_REGION_CLAUDE_3_5_HAIKU      VERTEX_REGION_CLAUDE_3_5_SONNET
+VERTEX_REGION_CLAUDE_3_7_SONNET     VERTEX_REGION_CLAUDE_4_0_OPUS
+VERTEX_REGION_CLAUDE_4_0_SONNET     VERTEX_REGION_CLAUDE_4_1_OPUS
+VERTEX_REGION_CLAUDE_4_5_OPUS       VERTEX_REGION_CLAUDE_4_5_SONNET
+VERTEX_REGION_CLAUDE_4_6_OPUS       VERTEX_REGION_CLAUDE_4_6_SONNET
+VERTEX_REGION_CLAUDE_4_7_OPUS       VERTEX_REGION_CLAUDE_4_8_OPUS
+VERTEX_REGION_CLAUDE_5_SONNET       VERTEX_REGION_CLAUDE_FABLE_5
+VERTEX_REGION_CLAUDE_HAIKU_4_5
+```
+
+**Meaning** : if you run in an AWS or GCP environment with the right
+env vars set, the extension can dispatch to Bedrock / Vertex instead
+of the Anthropic API directly. Regional model routing is now
+per-model-family, configurable via env.
+
+### 2. New model IDs
+
+Three ID namespaces, all catalogued in one place. Note the presence of
+**unshipped code-name models** (`mythos`, `fable`) — probably staged
+for future release.
+
+**Anthropic marketplace slug** (`anthropic.<slug>`) — 5 new :
+
+```
+anthropic.claude-fable-5
+anthropic.claude-haiku-4-5
+anthropic.claude-opus-4-7
+anthropic.claude-opus-4-8
+anthropic.claude-sonnet-5
+```
+
+**Kebab-case (CLI / SDK facing)** — 17 new (many historical too, now
+catalogued together for switching) :
+
+```
+claude-3-5-haiku    claude-3-5-sonnet    claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022
+claude-3-7-sonnet   claude-fable-5       claude-haiku-4-5
+claude-mythos-5     claude-opus-4        claude-opus-4-1
+claude-opus-4-5     claude-opus-4-5-20251101   claude-opus-4-7
+claude-opus-4-8     claude-sonnet-4      claude-sonnet-4-5
+claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929      claude-sonnet-4-6
+```
+
+**Bedrock-style** (`us.anthropic.<slug>`) — 15 new :
+
+```
+us.anthropic.claude-3-5-haiku-20241022-v1:0
+us.anthropic.claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022-v2:0
+us.anthropic.claude-3-7-sonnet-20250219-v1:0
+us.anthropic.claude-fable-5
+us.anthropic.claude-haiku-4-5-20251001-v1:0
+us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-1-20250805-v1:0
+us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-20250514-v1:0
+us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-5-20251101-v1:0
+us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-6-v1
+us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-7
+us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8
+us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-20250514-v1:0
+us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929-v1:0
+us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6
+us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-5
+```
+
+### 3. New feature keys
+
+Config values / capability flags introduced in the model dispatch
+plumbing :
+
+- `SSEHttpError` — new error class for server-sent-events streaming.
+  Probably distinguishes network-level failures from Anthropic API
+  errors (finer-grained retry logic).
+- `adaptive_thinking` — new thinking mode variant. Was
+  `default_on`/`off` previously ; now there's an adaptive third rail.
+- `context_management` — new capability toggle. Probably relates to
+  automatic context compaction / truncation.
+- `mid_conv_system` — mid-conversation system prompt handling.
+  Probably lets the ext inject a system prompt mid-stream instead of
+  only at conversation start.
+- `lean_prompt` — new prompt mode. Streamlined variant.
+- `fast_mode` — corresponds to the /fast Claude Code toggle. Probably
+  now surfaced as a first-class capability the model dispatcher can
+  see.
+- `overflow` — probably context-overflow handling policy.
+- `rejects_disabled_thinking` — flag distinguishing which models
+  refuse a request when `thinking: off` is passed.
+
+**Effort levels** — 3 new granularity constants :
+
+- `effort` (base)
+- `max_effort`
+- `xhigh_effort` (a step above max)
+
+Probably driving compute-budget control per request.
+
+**Model family labels** — 4 new bare strings :
+
+- `haiku`, `sonnet`, `mythos`, `fable`
+
+Match the 4 emerging model families. `mythos` and `fable` are the
+new code-names — not yet in the marketplace, but wired in the
+dispatcher.
+
+### 4. `native-binary/claude` bumped
+
+Size delta : 248 MB (v201) → 258 MB (v202) = **+10 MB**. Almost
+certainly the underlying Claude Code CLI binary got a version bump
+matching the ext version, with the same set of features baked in.
+
+## What did NOT change (surface confirmation)
+
+Verified explicit non-changes to reassure our patch-set stability :
+
+- `onDidReceiveMessage` chokepoint in `setupPanel()` — same shape (3
+  call sites, same regex captures `(panel, msg, comms)`).
+- `sendRequest(sid, req, abort)` signature — the requestId generator
+  function was renamed (`Y3()` on 2.1.145 → `Hs()` in 2.1.202), but
+  the surrounding structure is identical. Our patch already uses
+  `\w+\(\)` for the generator name so it survives.
+- `handleToolPermissionRequest` in the webview — same `Q = new Gn(…)`
+  ; same `Q.onResolved(…)` ; same
+  `this.permissionRequests.value.filter(…)` shape. The webview-side
+  intercept anchor is unchanged.
+- `class Gn` fields (`channelId`, `toolName`, `inputs`, `suggestions`,
+  `resolved`) and methods (`accept`, `reject`, `onResolved`) —
+  identical. Our `Q.accept(input, perms)` / `Q.reject(msg, false)`
+  contract holds.
+
+## Impact on our patches
+
+**None.** The 7 patches (5 pre-existing + 2 new) all apply cleanly on
+pristine v2.1.202 with zero syntax errors on both `extension.js` and
+`webview/index.js`. The version-adaptive naming in
+`icon-fix-open-in-current-panel.py` (step 1/6) switches the enum from
+`"primary"` to `"active-panel"` on 2.1.202+ — pure future-proofing
+against a hypothetical Anthropic wiring of `"primary"` that hasn't
+happened yet.
+
+## Compatibility with our devcontainer configs
+
+On 2.1.202+ the two config files below need updating **only when the
+image bumps to 2.1.202+** — currently we're on 2.1.145, no action
+required :
+
+- `.devcontainer/devcontainer.json` :
+  `"claudeCode.preferredLocation": "primary"` → `"active-panel"`
+- `.devcontainer/vscode-settings.jsonc` : same.
+
+The change is idempotent : if you set `"active-panel"` on a 2.1.145
+container, our patch on that version added `"primary"` to the enum
+(not `"active-panel"`) so VS Code will reject the setting as invalid.
+The migration is version-locked : bump image + config in the same PR.
